From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rvwasm <rvwasm@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:41:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] wasm: futex_atomic_cmpxchg_inatomic reports the value it
 found

The contract is: store the value found at uaddr in *uval and return 0,
whether or not it was oldval; callers compare. This one tried the strong
CAS 128 times and returned -EAGAIN on a mismatch without setting *uval, so
wake_futex_pi() could not tell a futex word that changed (-EAGAIN, retry)
from one with garbage in it (-EINVAL): a corrupt PI futex word made
futex_unlock_pi() retry for good. One strong compare-and-swap, which hands
back what it found.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/wasm/include/asm/futex.h | 27 ++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/include/asm/futex.h b/arch/wasm/include/asm/futex.h
index 05f901e..603895d 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/include/asm/futex.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/include/asm/futex.h
@@ -7,28 +7,25 @@
 #include <linux/uaccess.h>
 #include <asm/errno.h>
 
-#define FUTEX_MAX_LOOPS	128
-
+/*
+ * Store the value found at uaddr in *uval, and newval there if it was oldval;
+ * 0 either way (the callers compare *uval with oldval to tell). A value that
+ * was not oldval is not a failure: wake_futex_pi() tells a futex word that
+ * changed under it (-EAGAIN, try again) from one with garbage in it (-EINVAL)
+ * by what it found, and a word that never matched would be retried for good.
+ */
 static inline int futex_atomic_cmpxchg_inatomic(u32 *uval, u32 __user *uaddr,
 						u32 oldval, u32 newval)
 {
-	int loops;
-	u32 expected;
+	u32 expected = oldval;
 
 	if (!access_ok(uaddr, sizeof(u32)))
 		return -EFAULT;
 
-	for (loops = 0; loops < FUTEX_MAX_LOOPS; ++loops) {
-		expected = oldval;
-		if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n((volatile u32 *)uaddr,
-				&expected, newval, false, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST,
-				__ATOMIC_RELAXED)) {
-			*uval = oldval;
-			return 0;
-		}
-	}
-
-	return -EAGAIN;
+	__atomic_compare_exchange_n((volatile u32 *)uaddr, &expected, newval,
+				    false, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
+	*uval = expected;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static inline int arch_futex_atomic_op_inuser(int op, u32 oparg, int *oval,
